{"status":"dry","notes":"The API worked with no 429s, but the data is thin. Searching 因美納 and 因美納台灣生物科技 returned 3 award notices, all won by Illumina Taiwan (90807364) from one buyer, the National Health Research Institutes (NHRI). They were 2022-09-20 (TruSight Oncology 500, 2 sets), 2023-02-01 (COVIDSeq, 1 batch) and 2023-12-21 (NovaSeq 6000 S4 v1.5 300-cycle, 16 sets). The last of these is Illumina's own Taiwan entity buying the 6000, and it predates the thesis window. Searching Element Biosciences returned 1 tender with two corrected-notice records (2024-12-05 and 2024-12-06). The buyer was Academia Sinica, which bought one AVITI24 spatial multi-omics platform, job BRCAS11347, with the winning bidder listed as Element Biosciences, Inc. (U0061260). No award values appear in any record. I found no 2025+ records, no competitive loss or price data, and no Illumina-vs-Element head-to-head. Illumina mostly sells through distributors in Taiwan, so direct awards say little about vendor share. I read the pages through a summarizing fetch, not raw JSON, so the details come from that summary.","how_to_mine":"Not worth a deep extraction. If revisited, use the raw JSON with the job numbers (112A0C0676, BRCAS11347) to fetch full tender details and amounts, then search distributor names such as Illumina's Taiwan resellers for 2025-26 NovaSeq X award prices.","difficulty":"easy","items":[{"label":"2B","direction":"supports","claim":"An academic buyer in Taiwan bought Element's AVITI24 directly, in a tender titled for AVITI24.","detail":"Academia Sinica's tender BRCAS11347 (corrected award notices dated 2024-12-05 and 2024-12-06) went to Element Biosciences, Inc. for one AVITI24 spatial multi-omics sequencing platform. No value is disclosed. This is a single research-institution placement, and the platform is aimed at spatial work, not high-throughput consumables.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/searchbycompanyname?query=Element Biosciences","date":"2024-12-06","source_n